        "original_id": "9f48bd24-1275-56ce-a0a3-c14046fabcae",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Fianna Éireann, Sinn Féin, Fianna Fáil, British House of Commons, Dáil Éireann\n- People: Constance Markievicz, Bulmer Hobson\n- Roles: politician, revolutionary nationalist, suffragette, socialist\n\nFacts:\n- Fianna Éireann is an Irish nationalist youth organisation founded in 1909 by Bulmer Hobson and Constance Markievicz.\n- Constance Georgine Markievicz, also known as Countess Markievicz and née Gore-Booth, was born on 4 February 1868 and died on 15 July 1927.\n- Constance Markievicz was an Irish Sinn Féin and Fianna Fáil politician, revolutionary nationalist, suffragette, and socialist.\n- In December 1918, Constance Markievicz became the first woman elected to the British House of Commons.\n- Constance Markievicz did not take her seat in the British House of Commons and instead, with other Sinn Féin TDs, formed the first Dáil Éireann.",
